#N canvas 40 40 1360 1000 12;
#X text 20 20 g_led -- the aux button LED \, and its sole owner. The only state display in the rig that is not a screen. Callers send SEMANTICS on the disp bus -- led running -- and never a colour \, exactly as they do for the OLED. Same rule \, different surface: one writer \, one display., f 58;
#X text 20 130 creation args: none. inlets: none. outlets: none., f 58;
#X obj 20 240 r disp;
#X obj 20 290 route led;
#X obj 20 360 route off stopped running panic;
#X msg 20 440 0;
#X msg 180 440 5;
#X msg 340 440 3;
#X msg 500 440 1;
#X obj 20 530 s led;
#X obj 760 400 list append;
#X obj 760 450 t b;
#X msg 760 500 warn g_led unknown-led-state;
#X obj 760 560 s err;
#X text 20 620 THE STATE TABLE IS THIS ROUTE BOX \, and it is the whole abstraction. mother takes 0-7 and gives off \, red \, yellow \, green \, cyan \, dark blue \, pink \, white -- so stopped is 5 and running is 3. STOPPED IS LIT RATHER THAN DARK on purpose: a stopped patch and a patch that has died look identical if stopped is off., f 58;
#X text 20 740 led IS A RESERVED disp SELECTOR. g_oled matches it and throws it away \, which is what stops an LED request drawing as a nonsense parameter row -- everything g_oled does not recognise is a parameter by definition. Adding a selector there is a deliberate edit \; see ref-conventions.md \, The display bus., f 58;
#X text 760 240 NO list append BEFORE THE SECOND ROUTE \, and that is not an oversight. route matches a SELECTOR \, and led running arrives out of the first route with running already AS the selector -- the shape the second route wants. A list append here would break every match., f 44;
#X text 760 640 THE REJECT BRANCH DOES NEED ONE. A reject carries the message it did not match \, so a bare symbol reaches the trigger and Pd says: can only convert 's' to 'b'. list append makes it a list \, which trigger will convert. Same family as the three route traps., f 44;
#X text 20 880 mother already sets led 0 on quitting \, so the safe exit needs nothing here. It also applies % 8 \, so no value out of this file can be illegal -- but every value out of this file is one of four., f 58;
#X connect 2 0 3 0;
#X connect 3 0 4 0;
#X connect 4 0 5 0;
#X connect 4 1 6 0;
#X connect 4 2 7 0;
#X connect 4 3 8 0;
#X connect 4 4 10 0;
#X connect 5 0 9 0;
#X connect 6 0 9 0;
#X connect 7 0 9 0;
#X connect 8 0 9 0;
#X connect 10 0 11 0;
#X connect 11 0 12 0;
#X connect 12 0 13 0;
